# Generated from analysis/generated/symbols.json for pinned MesenCE.
# Native syntax: MemoryType:HEX_ADDRESS:Label[:Comment].
SnesPrgRom:0C41:Text_TestCharacterMetadataBit7:Shared helper reached from four text/layout loops including `03:8998`, `00:C4CB`, and `00:C510`. It indexes the byte table at `00:C6F8` by character code and tests bit 7. Printable-table inspection shows uppercase A-Z in the low half while lowercase a-z, digits and much punctuation usually carry bit 7; therefore this is a verified character-metadata class test, not yet a proven glyph-width flag.
SnesPrgRom:B8F1:RNC1_Unpack:Identified by unique opcode-structure match to preserved 1992 SNES `RNC_1.S`; ROM offset `0x00B8F1`. Regional/build equivalents: Europe retail `01:B8E2` (`0x00B8E2`), 1994-11-29 PAL prototype `01:B8D1` (`0x00B8D1`), legacy beta identical to USA.
SnesPrgRom:BB60:RNC1_MakeHuffTail:Preserved Method-1 MAKEHUFF tail begins here; final RTS at `01:BB6E`, establishing the shipped generic RNC1 body end.
SnesPrgRom:BB6F:RNC1_ReadWordLoROMSafe:Integration helper used by the shipped Method-1 decoder for a 16-bit packed-stream read through `IN`. Normal path returns `LDA [IN]` while restoring the pointer; when `IN=$FFFF`, it fetches the high byte from next-bank `$8000`, matching LoROM linear-stream continuity across a bank boundary. `01:BB73` is the helper's wrap-test `BNE`, not a store.
SnesPrgRom:C5AF:HUD_QueueMessage:Nitrodon's annotated stunt disassembly shows this long-call target receiving message IDs for Wipeout (`0x0E`), Head Bounce (`0x10`), Tabletop (`0x11`), flip/roll/twist/Z-flip result messages, and praise messages. Exact queue/render split still needs local call-graph validation.
SnesPrgRom:1007E:APU_UploadBlockById_Wrapper:Exact bytes `JSR $8082; RTL`. Callers load X with audio block IDs before entering; the body at `02:8082` performs the SPC handshake and calls `APU_ResolveBlockPointer` at `02:812A`, establishing X as a block-record selector.
SnesPrgRom:1012A:APU_ResolveBlockPointer:Exact static routine maps block ID X onto the packed audio-record pool beginning at `10:8000`. It walks X length-prefixed records, performing LoROM bank-wrap arithmetic, and returns the selected record pointer in DP `$63-$65`. Package-table IDs `$00-$31` address the first 50 records, but direct setup calls pass IDs through at least `$42`; the same contiguous parser resolves records `$32-$42`. Therefore `$00-$31` is the package-table ID universe, not the resolver's upper bound.
SnesPrgRom:11A42:Stunt_FinalizeAndScoreAirTricks:Nitrodon's focused `stunts.txt` plus bank-82 listing expose the complete landing/finalization pipeline: roll/flip quarter-turn accumulation, half-twist conversion, Z-flip/tabletop handling, wipeout/headbounce checks, trick-message selection, stunt-combination indexing, praise lookup, and reset of transient stunt state.
SnesPrgRom:12968:Player_ApplyVerticalAcceleration:Nitrodon's bank-82 annotation is directly supported by the instruction flow: current-player Y velocity is capped below `0x0200`, upward motion receives +19, downward acceleration is `19 - Yvel/32`, the result is added to Y velocity, and current-player Y coordinate is incremented.
SnesPrgRom:12A6E:Input_DecodePlayer1Buttons:Nitrodon's bank-82 listing shows raw controller words `$030D/$030F` decoded into explicit A/X/L/R/B/Y/select/start flags and normalized vertical/horizontal direction fields at `$0311/$0315`.
SnesPrgRom:18971:Text_HandleFCPositionControl:Bounded static analysis of the Sayans translation-control grammar. The routine preserves A, recognizes low-byte `FC`, consumes the following parameter, scans subsequent character bytes until `FF` or `FB`, consults `Text_TestCharacterMetadataBit7` for ordinary bytes, then computes `parameter * 32 + horizontal adjustment` into DP `$9F`. The 32-column arithmetic and translated `FF FC xx` / `FB FC xx` sequences support a centered tilemap-position/layout role. Exact user-facing meaning of the parameter remains unpromoted.
SnesWorkRam:000E:Frontend_SelectedRow:Recovered bot label; native route captures row `0x00` through the verified clean frontend route. Exact semantics outside these menus not yet tested.
SnesWorkRam:009B:Frontend_SelectedOption:Recovered bot uses it for main-menu/tour selection. Native captures show `0x00` at clean main menu and first tours page, consistent with bot policy.
SnesWorkRam:009F:Frontend_CurrentMenu:Verified in both native and Snes9x/snesref deterministic runs: `0xD7` main menu, `0x3C` one-player rider select, `0x6D` first one-player tours page, `0xF6` one-player track select, `0x16` now-playing screen, then `0x00` after race entry.
SnesWorkRam:0313:Race_ActiveState:Recovered bot label `inRace`; verified as `0x01` after deterministic race entry in both native and Snes9x/snesref runs. Non-race screens can contain other transient values, so only `0x01 = active race` is currently asserted.
SnesWorkRam:033B:Player1_FacingAtTakeoff:Nitrodon's map says this records whether the racer was facing right when leaving the ground. The stunt finalizer uses it to decide whether accumulated quarter-turn direction maps to flip versus roll; paired player-2 slot is `$033D`.
SnesWorkRam:0411:Player1_XPosition:Effective recovered-bot word key `xPos`. Race-acceleration run 36512546762 moves it identically in native/reference from 1088 at rest to 1655 under staged Right input, alongside positive X speed.
SnesWorkRam:0413:Player2_XPosition:Dessyreqt's recovered Tabletop bot and `Races2.wch` use this as player-2 X position; paired structure with verified player-1 `$0411` and the existing player-2 pitch/copy routines supports the assignment. Dynamic 2P causal validation remains desirable.
SnesWorkRam:0415:Player1_YPosition:Effective recovered-bot word key `yPos`. Sustained-B run 36514981164 causally changes player 1 from ground Y=859 in the matched no-B control to Y=797 while airborne; native and Snes9x match exactly.
SnesWorkRam:0417:Player2_YPosition:Dessyreqt's recovered Tabletop bot and `Races2.wch` use this as player-2 Y position; it is the paired word after verified player-1 `$0415`. Dynamic 2P causal validation remains desirable.
SnesWorkRam:042B:Player1_ZFlipCount:Nitrodon's map identifies the player-specific slot as Z-flip count. Bank-82 code reads/writes it under 16-bit accumulator mode, caps the landing result at 4, and uses it directly in the stunt-combination index. USJO v8 reads only the low byte.
SnesWorkRam:042D:Player2_ZFlipCount:Nitrodon's WRAM map identifies the paired player-2 Z-flip field; Dessyreqt's `Races2.wch` independently labels it Z-Flips.
SnesWorkRam:042F:Player1_TabletopDuration:Nitrodon's map and annotated bank-82 code identify this as tabletop duration; `INC $042F,X` at `02:9582` advances it and `02:9C87` requires duration >= 3 to emit the Tabletop message. Dynamic run 36776825024 independently observes X input driving low-byte `0→1→2→3→4→0` at a two-frame cadence in native and pinned Snes9x. This supersedes the older accumulated-count label.
SnesWorkRam:0431:Player2_TabletopDuration:Nitrodon's WRAM map identifies player-2 tabletop duration here; Dessyreqt's Tabletop bot and `Races2.wch` independently use the same paired address.
SnesWorkRam:04B7:Player1_XSpeed:Effective recovered-bot word key `xSpeed`; bot explicitly sign-converts it. Race-acceleration run 36512546762 changes it identically from 0 to +447 under Right input while X position increases.
SnesWorkRam:04B9:Player2_XSpeed:Dessyreqt's recovered Tabletop bot and `Races2.wch` use this as player-2 X speed, paired with verified player-1 `$04B7`.
SnesWorkRam:04BB:Player1_YSpeed:Effective recovered-bot word key `ySpeed`; bot sign-converts it. In run 36514981164 sustained B changes it causally from 0 in the matched control to -21 while player 1 is airborne; native and Snes9x match exactly.
SnesWorkRam:04BD:Player2_YSpeed:Dessyreqt's recovered Tabletop bot and `Races2.wch` use this as player-2 Y speed, paired with verified player-1 `$04BB`.
SnesWorkRam:04C7:Player1_PitchAngle:Persistent player-1 pitch/orientation. From control angle `0x07`, eight L frames produce `0x37` (= 7−16 mod 64) and eight R frames produce `0x17` (= 7+16 mod 64), identically native/reference. ROM `02:8D84` copies working `$0F49` into this slot.
SnesWorkRam:04C9:Player2_PitchAngle:Paired player-2 pitch/orientation slot. Sibling ROM routine at `02:9272` executes `LDY $0F49; STY $04C9`; surrounding destinations shift coherently to player-2 fields.
SnesWorkRam:04F5:Player1_CameraXSpeed:Nitrodon's map calls this player-1 camera X velocity; Dessyreqt's `Races.wch` and SCUM independently use it as Camera X Speed. SCUM sign-converts the byte.
SnesWorkRam:04F7:Player2_CameraXSpeed:Dessyreqt's `Races2.wch` identifies this paired player-2 Camera X Speed slot. Pairing with corroborated player-1 `$04F5` is strong, but direct runtime validation is still open.
SnesWorkRam:0545:Player1_AirTime:Dynamic run 36514981164 causally changes the low byte from 0 to 9 under sustained B while Y position/speed enter the airborne trajectory. Nitrodon's WRAM map identifies the slot as time in air with a 9-frame maximum, and bank-82 stunt code reads it as a word (`LDA $0545,Y`). Historical bots read only the low byte.
SnesWorkRam:0BA1:Player1_FacedDirection:Recovered bot: 1 = right, 0 = left. Not yet independently validated.
SnesWorkRam:0BA3:Player2_FacedDirection:Independently present in Nitrodon's WRAM map and Dessyreqt's recovered Tabletop bot as player-2 facing; historical convention is 1 = right, 0 = left.
SnesWorkRam:0C63:Frontend_SelectedColumn:Recovered bot label; native captures change with frontend scene/selection. Rider-select ready state captures `0x06`, matching the bot's left-column target value.
SnesWorkRam:0DFD:Player1_ZRotationState:Static scan run 36769525945 exposes paired copy structure: `02:8AB2` loads `$0DFD` and stores it to shared working `$0F57`, while `02:8FBA` loads paired `$0DFF` into the same working slot and `02:8DB2` copies `$0F57` back to `$0DFD`. This strongly supports `$0DFD/$0DFF` as paired persistent racer Z-state slots; exact physical interpretation remains open.
SnesWorkRam:0EF1:Player1_LapsRemaining:Nitrodon's map identifies laps remaining; paired player-2 slot is `$0EF3`.
SnesWorkRam:0F49:CurrentPlayer_PitchScratch:Historical bot reads this as `pitch`, but static sibling routines copy the same working value into persistent player-1 `$04C7` or player-2 `$04C9` slots. L-vs-control checkpoints leave `$0F49` unchanged while `$04C7` changes causally, so it should not be treated as stable player-1 storage.
SnesWorkRam:0F57:CurrentPlayer_ZRotationWorking:Static scan run 36769525945 shows `$0F57` as shared current-player working state: `02:8AB2` copies player-1 `$0DFD` into it, `02:8FBA` copies paired `$0DFF` into it, `02:8DB2` writes it back to `$0DFD`, and later bank-02 code mutates/clears it. USJO v8 calls the low byte `zprerotation`; exact physical semantics remain open.
SnesWorkRam:0F61:CurrentPlayer_HalfTwistCount:Nitrodon's map identifies this as the current-player number of half-twists. The stunt finalizer at `02:9C2E` shifts it right once to derive full twists, caps the result at 4, and feeds that into the stunt-combination index. Writer analysis independently shows current-player copy/clear/increment behavior.
SnesWorkRam:0F9F:CurrentPlayer_XVelocityWorking:Nitrodon's map identifies current-player X velocity here. Bank-81 collision/transform code reads `$0F9F/$0FA1`, transforms both through matrix terms, and stores the new X/Y pair back; bank-82 movement and boost paths also mutate `$0F9F`. This resolves USJO's old “alternative speed” comment as shared current-player working state rather than a second player-1 field.
SnesWorkRam:0FA1:CurrentPlayer_YVelocityWorking:Nitrodon's map and bank-81 velocity transform pair this with `$0F9F`; bank-82 vertical-acceleration code at `02:A968` updates this slot directly.
SnesWorkRam:0FCB:Player1_ArrowDirection:Effective duplicate-key address used by recovered bot; 0 = right, 1 = left.
SnesWorkRam:0FCC:Player1_ArrowsVisible:Effective duplicate-key address used by recovered bot; 0 means direction arrows showing.
SnesWorkRam:0FEF:CurrentPlayer_Index:Nitrodon's map records `0 = player 1`, `2 = player 2`. Bank-82 stunt/movement code repeatedly loads it into X/Y to index paired 16-bit player slots.
SnesWorkRam:1199:Player1_NextCheckpoint:Nitrodon's map identifies the next-checkpoint field; paired player-2 slot is `$119B`. High-value race-finish fixture target.
SnesWorkRam:119B:Player2_NextCheckpoint:Nitrodon's WRAM map and Dessyreqt's `Races2.wch` independently identify the paired player-2 checkpoint slot.
SnesWorkRam:119D:Player1_FinishGateState:Nitrodon's map records `0` when player 1 can cross the finish line; paired player-2 slot is `$119F`. Exact nonzero state meanings remain open.
SnesWorkRam:11BA:Race_CountdownTimer:Recovered bot word key shared by players. In run 36512546762 it decreases identically in native/reference by exactly `0x0100` per guest frame across the staged pre-start/acceleration checkpoints. Exact game-facing units/threshold meanings remain to be named.
SnesWorkRam:11CD:CurrentPlayer_BoostMeterWorking:Nitrodon's map distinguishes this shared current-player boost meter from stable player slots at `$11CF/$11D1`. Bank-82 code zeroes it on wipeout, subtracts 16 in an off-screen penalty path, clamps computed boost to `0x0180`, and feeds half the value into velocity limiting. USJO v8 reads only its low byte as a zero/nonzero gate.
SnesWorkRam:11CF:Player1_BoostMeter:Nitrodon's map identifies the stable player-1 boost slot, distinct from shared current-player working `$11CD`. Local copy-in/copy-out path should still be named explicitly.
SnesWorkRam:11D1:Player2_BoostMeter:Nitrodon's map identifies the paired player-2 boost slot.
SnesWorkRam:11F9:Player1_RollCount:Nitrodon's map explicitly records a 2-byte player-1 roll count. The stunt routine increments it with 16-bit `INC $11F9,X` after four quarter-turn progress steps, and may credit a 3/4 roll on landing. USJO v8 reads only the low byte.
SnesWorkRam:11FB:Player2_RollCount:Nitrodon's WRAM map identifies a two-byte player-2 roll count; Dessyreqt's `Races2.wch` independently labels the same address Rolls.
SnesWorkRam:11FD:Player1_FlipCount:Nitrodon's map explicitly records a 2-byte player-1 flip count. The stunt routine increments it with 16-bit `INC $11FD,X` after four quarter-turn progress steps, and may credit a 3/4 flip on landing. USJO v8 reads only the low byte.
SnesWorkRam:11FF:Player2_FlipCount:Nitrodon's WRAM map identifies a two-byte player-2 flip count; Dessyreqt's `Races2.wch` independently labels the same address Flips.
SnesWorkRam:1201:Player1_RollQuarterProgress:Bank-82 stunt code increments this progress value and converts it into one roll when it reaches 4, then resets it; paired player-2 slot is `$1203`.
SnesWorkRam:1205:Player1_FlipQuarterProgress:Bank-82 stunt code increments this progress value and converts it into one flip when it reaches 4, then resets it; paired player-2 slot is `$1207`.
SnesWorkRam:12AF:Stunt_CurrentScore:Nitrodon's map identifies the current score on stunt tracks. Score update semantics remain to be traced.
SnesWorkRam:132B:Race_ReverseControls:Recovered bot: 2 = controls reversed, 0 = normal. Not yet independently validated.
SnesWorkRam:1361:Player1_StuntAirLatch:Olivier retained this as an “Air flag”; Nitrodon's stunt disassembly shows `02:9A97` setting indexed `$1361` to 1 during stunt-air initialization and `02:9D88` clearing it during finalization. Exact relationship to ordinary air-time `$0545` remains open.
SnesWorkRam:1509:Camera_ScreenXPosition:Historical TAS watch list labels this “Screen X Position.” Not consumed by v8; local camera/unit semantics still need validation.
SnesWorkRam:10000:Course_ActiveDecodedPayload:Confirmed by run 36514985916: active Dragster decoded stream 1 matches 33,814/33,815 bytes from this address; only decoded byte 11 is runtime-mutated.
